@startuml agent_metadata_gaussdb_model
!pragma layout elk
title Agent Metadata GaussDB Tables
top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam ArrowColor #53657D
skinparam ClassBorderColor #53657D
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #F7F9FC
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

' Source evidence:
' - Repository-relative path, Git-escaped:
'   "AGENT\345\205\203\346\225\260\346\215\256\350\256\276\350\256\241.json":2-46.
' - Fields at lines 2-20 map to agent_metadata.
' - Arrays at lines 10 and 21-35 map to ordered child tables.
' - Permission arrays at lines 36-46 map to one effect row per tool.
' Observed behavior: the current JSON is a current-state Agent resource with a
' monotonically increasing version and no separate history resource.
' Design reason: fixed scalar and system prompt fields use typed columns, while
' repeated arrays use child tables for uniqueness, filtering, and stable order.
' Product constraint: only the fields present in the current JSON are persisted.
' GaussDB divergence: physical foreign keys are optional because GaussDB
' Distributed does not support them; the base DDL uses logical relationships.

class agent_metadata <<current Agent>> {
  agent_id: VARCHAR PK
  resource_type: VARCHAR
  version: BIGINT
  name: VARCHAR UK
  display_name: VARCHAR
  description: TEXT
  system_role: TEXT
  system_objective: TEXT
  system_instructions: TEXT
  system_tool_policy: TEXT
  system_safety: TEXT
  system_completion: TEXT
  system_response_style: TEXT
  system_example: TEXT?
  created_at: TIMESTAMPTZ
  updated_at: TIMESTAMPTZ
}

class agent_model <<models>> {
  agent_id: VARCHAR PK
  model_id: VARCHAR PK
  sort_order: INTEGER UK
}

class agent_use_case <<use_cases>> {
  agent_id: VARCHAR PK
  sort_order: INTEGER PK
  use_case: TEXT
}

class agent_tool_binding <<binding_tools>> {
  agent_id: VARCHAR PK
  tool_id: VARCHAR PK
  tool_version: BIGINT?
  sort_order: INTEGER UK
}

class agent_skill_binding <<binding_skills>> {
  agent_id: VARCHAR PK
  skill_id: VARCHAR PK
  skill_version: BIGINT?
  sort_order: INTEGER UK
}

class agent_tool_permission <<permission>> {
  agent_id: VARCHAR PK
  tool_id: VARCHAR PK
  permission_effect: deny | ask | allow
}

agent_metadata *-- "1..*" agent_model : has
agent_metadata *-- "0..*" agent_use_case : describes
agent_metadata *-- "0..*" agent_tool_binding : binds
agent_metadata *-- "0..*" agent_skill_binding : binds
agent_metadata *-- "0..*" agent_tool_permission : governs

note right of agent_metadata
version is the optimistic-lock value.
Every successful metadata update increments it once.
end note

note right of agent_tool_binding
NULL tool_version means latest.
The same rule applies to skill_version.
end note

note bottom of agent_tool_permission
One row replaces the three JSON arrays.
The primary key prevents conflicting effects
for the same Agent and Tool.
end note

note bottom of agent_metadata
Base DDL omits physical foreign keys for
GaussDB Distributed compatibility.
The service writes the root and child rows
in one transaction.
end note

@enduml
